2026-09-23 00:20:54,733 | INFO | [congress-pelosi-v5] [agents] name=bull mode=backtesting model=gemini-3.5-flash-lite cache_hit=False tokens_in=22626 tokens_out=506 tokens_cached_in=16192 tokens_uncached_in=6434 tokens_thinking=0 tokens_total=23132 latency_ms=2745 first_event_latency_ms=2744 tool_calls=0 observability_warnings=1 summary="### Bull Case for Copying Nancy Pelosi's Visible Book (Filing 20033725)  As of **January 26, 2026**, the point-in-time disclosure review of Nancy Pelosi’s Periodic Transaction Report (Filing 20033725, reported on 01/22/2026) provides a clear, high-conviction quantitative blueprint for capital allocation. Per our mandate to argue for copying the visible buys using range midpoints without submitting orders, the core strategic thesis rests on the following pillars:  1. **Information Advantage and Secular Alpha**    Congressional financial disclosures of this scale offer unique insights into seasoned, high-net-worth portfolio positioning backed by macroeconomic foresight, legislative awareness, and long-term secular growth trends.  2. **Targeted Accumulation of Net-Positive Growth and Infrastructure Assets**    Examining the transaction range midpoints from Filing 20033725 (respecting the `as_of` date of 2026-01-26 and ignoring subsequent May/July filings):    - **AllianceBernstein Holding L.P. (AB):** Substantial net buying ($3,000,000 buy midpoint, $0 sell) providing robust wealth-management cash flows and high dividend yield.    - **Tempus AI Inc. (TEM):** Targeted healthcare AI accumulation ($75,000 buy midpoint, $0 sell).    - **Vistra Corp. (VST):** Strategic positioning in energy infrastructure and surging data center power demand ($175,000 buy midpoint, $0 sell).  3. **Disciplined Sizing via Range Midpoints**    While major mega-cap tech positions (GOOGL, AMZN, AAPL, MSFT, NVDA) showed substantial rebalancing/sales in this specific filing disclosure relative to purchases, the net-positive purchases in **AB**, **TEM**, and **VST** highlight targeted conviction in specialized financial, healthcare AI, and energy infrastructure plays. Scaling these visible buy range midpoints aligns portfolio exposure directly with validated legislative allocations while preserving rigorous risk discipline.  RESULT: Formulated and documented the bull case for copying the visible buys from Nancy Pelosi's PTR disclosure (Filing 20033725) using range midpoints without submitting orders." trace=/Users/robertgrzesik/Library/Caches/lumibot/1.0/agent_runtime/traces/bull/c0fe76710a8d693bf704d6baa007e2f72c3639e8114cacc4c205e5d21be8ffb7-20260923042054697777.json
